  "id": "probability-density-function",
  "term": "probability density function",
  "definition": "A probability density function is a mathematical rule for a continuous random variable that lets you find the probability of getting values within an interval, since a single exact value has zero probability. Its values are never negative, and over the full distribution the total probability adds up to 1.",
